---
module: concepts
func_id: extract-defined-concepts
---

***conformance tests***

# one-concept
The text `- ⟨Task⟩ is a thing to do.` defines [⟨Task⟩] with no error.

# several-concepts
The text `- ⟨A⟩, ⟨B⟩ are twins.` defines [⟨A⟩, ⟨B⟩] with no error.

***acceptance tests***

# invalid-name
The text `- ⟨Bad name⟩ is x.` defines nothing and gives the error `Syntax error: Invalid concept: ⟨Bad name⟩. Should contain only letters, numbers, hyphens and dots.`.

# no-concept
The text `- A plain sentence.` defines nothing and gives one error starting with `Syntax error: Invalid definition specification text: - A plain sentence.`.
